#
# Why this file claims nobody
# ---------------------------
# It previously named six teams — @eruofood/maintainers, /backend, /frontend,
# /mobile, /platform — and GitHub rejected every one of them. `GET /repos/
# nzebrian/eruofood-ai/codeowners/errors` returned 8 "Unknown owner" errors,
# one per reference.
#
# That was not a typo. `nzebrian/eruofood-ai` is owned by a **user account**
# (`owner.type: "User"`), and GitHub teams exist only inside organizations. The
# `@eruofood/*` handles could not be created even if somebody wanted to. The
# file had been asserting an ownership structure that has never existed.
#
# A CODEOWNERS file full of unresolvable owners is worse than an empty one. It
# reads, to anyone opening it, as though review routing is configured. Enable
# "require review from Code Owners" against it and the rule matches owners who
# cannot approve, so it either blocks every pull request or silently enforces
# nothing — and which of those you get is not obvious until you try it.
#
# So the rules are commented out. The file is syntactically valid, resolves
# zero owners, and claims nothing. `codeowners/errors` returns empty.
#
# What has to happen before these are enabled
# -------------------------------------------
# 1. Decide whether the repository moves to a GitHub organization. Teams
#    (`@org/team`) require one. Under a personal account, CODEOWNERS may name
#    **individual usernames only**.
# 2. Obtain the real handles. Every `<OWNER:...>` token below is an unresolved
#    input owned by the repository administrator. Do not guess them, and do not
#    substitute the repository owner's own handle merely to make the file
#    resolve — an owner who is always the pull request author cannot review it.
# 3. Give each named owner **write access**. GitHub ignores a code owner who
#    cannot push to the repository, without telling you.
# 4. Uncomment the rules, replace the tokens, and verify with
#    `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/codeowners/errors` — it must return zero errors.
# 5. Only then set `require_code_owner_review: true` in the `main` ruleset.
#
# `apps/api/scripts/verify_repository_governance.php` reports every remaining
# placeholder, and refuses to call CODEOWNER routing configured while any
# survives. See `.github/governance/APPLY_GOVERNANCE.md` for the full sequence.
#
